# core.autocrlf=true on the Windows dev box would otherwise check these out
# with CRLF. Anything that a Linux kernel, shell or cloud-init has to parse
# must stay LF: a shebang followed by \r fails with a baffling
# "no such file or directory", and cloud-init silently skips CRLF YAML.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
